          ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{2}{x0}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x0.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=1\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x0}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot\\left(1\\,\\text{d}u\\right) \\\\ & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\ & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x0|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
